  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_ec1d458339104b2bb45845651a92581b",
      "statement": "The report route resolves the school and membership contract first, then gates on `resolveTrustedRole` over `profiles.role` (never `resolveRouteRole`, whose `?role=` override would bypass it) and redirects a trainer to `/trainer` before either the batch or the roster fetch. When the profile snapshot is not `ok` the derived role is null, so the gate is skipped and the page runs on rather than denying.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/(dashboard)/t/%5BtenantCode%5D/(sections)/report/page.tsx#L34-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2971e2a19e3f961361aa5dcecb33d1300191ecd9d2b7e39f98a4faa4dc98cc12:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://modules/batches/data/learners.ts#L257-L264",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f6eb76e4ea11eff9cb02e11efcab93d7c07faad9ed2550d4ad0ca470570fb753:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_923391d4e4a44d5e91713cb5f2fa15d9",
      "statement": "The route reuses the profile snapshot it already holds for the membership verdict and folds it in with `withTenantAccess`, and combines `snapshot.status === 'sync-failed' || rosterSnapshot.status === 'sync-failed'` into one flag rendered as a `SyncFailedCallout` above both the empty branch and the populated report, so a failed roster still renders a partial, roster-blank report instead of a hidden one.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/(dashboard)/t/%5BtenantCode%5D/(sections)/report/page.tsx#L60-L100",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:26789019da07dfcae4e02d645fa64e7a82fde7f4055f53be509425d1e2916e2e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7ee99255bd3643eea2f6e0fa67521337",
      "statement": "`getTenantRosterSnapshot` keys the roster by `batch_code` and `attachRoster` hangs scholars and T2MIS facts on the batch only when that key exists, leaving a batch with no roster unchanged — so a partial read degrades into a thin report rather than an error.",
